ay","source":"https://www.mimslyninn.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","romance","senior"],"booking_route":"rooms via Mews (app.mews.com); dining booking not observed; phone 540.743.5105","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","eat"],"draw_rank":47,"blurb":"historic 45-room inn at 401 W. Main Street with two restaurants serving Southern cuisine and a bar stocked with local hand-crafted spirits"},{"name":"Downtown Harrisonburg Culinary District","source":"https://visitharrisonburgva.com/dining/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","culture","group"],"booking_route":"not observed","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":48,"blurb":"per the Harrisonburg visitor bureau, Virginia''s first culinary district, with over 80 locally owned restaurants downtown"},{"name":"Courtyard by Marriott Harrisonburg","source":"https://www.jmu.edu/admissions/visit/accommodations.shtml","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","hiking"],"booking_route":"marriott.com (brand booking; not fetched) or phone 540-432-3031","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":60,"blurb":"Listed by James Madison University among Harrisonburg visitor hotels as \"Courtyard Marriott\", 1890 Evelyn Bird Avenue, Harrisonburg, VA 22801, 540-432-3031; Harrisonburg is a gateway city west of the park''s Swift Run Gap entrance. The brand''s own page was not fetched; distance not stated on the page read"},{"name":"Residence Inn Harrisonburg","source":"https://www.jmu.edu/admissions/visit/accommodations.shtml","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","group"],"booking_route":"marriott.com (brand booking; not fetched) or phone 540-437-7426","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":61,"blurb":"Listed by James Madison University as \"Residence Inn: Harrisonburg\", 1945 Deyerle Avenue, Harrisonburg, VA 22801, 540-437-7426 - Marriott''s extended-stay brand. The brand''s own page was not fetched; distance not stated on the page read"},{"name":"DoubleTree by Hilton Harrisonburg","source":"https://www.jmu.edu/admissions/visit/accommodations.shtml","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","group"],"booking_route":"hilton.com (brand booking; not fetched) or phone 540-433-2521","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":62,"blurb":"Listed by James Madison University as \"DoubleTree by Hilton Harrisonburg\", 1400 East Market Street, Harrisonburg, 540-433-2521. The brand''s own page was not fetched; distance not stated on the page read"},{"name":"Hyatt Place Harrisonburg","source":"https://www.jmu.edu/admissions/visit/accommodations.shtml","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"hyatt.com (brand booking; not fetched) or phone 540-417-1234","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":63,"blurb":"Listed by James Madison University as \"Hyatt Place Harrisonburg\", 1884 Evelyn Byrd Avenue, Harrisonburg, VA 22801, 540-417-1234. The brand''s own page was not fetched; distance not stated on the page read"},{"name":"Hotel Madison, Harrisonburg","source":"https://www.hotelmadison.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["senior","culinary","group"],"booking_route":"own website booking; phone 540-564-0200 (JMU listing)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","eat"],"draw_rank":64,"blurb":"\"a charming boutique hotel with on-site restaurant, pool and other amenities, it is adjacent to the JMU campus and a short walk from historic downtown Harrisonburg\" (Harrisonburg tourism); its own site, 710 S. Main Street, names Monty''s Restaurant and Grace+Main Cafe and states no brand affiliation"},{"name":"Backcountry food storage kit: bear canister or bear-bag hang","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/planyourvisit/food-storage.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","expedition"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":65,"blurb":"The NPS tells backcountry campers: \"Store your canister on level ground at least 70-100 yards from your campsite.\" For a hang: \"You''ll need 50-100 feet of rope and a waterproof bag big enough to hold all of your food and scented items. Bear bags need to be suspended at least 12 feet above the ground and 6 feet away from the trunk and branches of the tree.\""},{"name":"Water filter or purification tablets for the trail","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/planyourvisit/drinking-water.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":66,"blurb":"The NPS: \"With the exception of developed water fountains and marked water spigots within the Park, all water should be purified before it is used for drinking\"; \"boil it for at least two minutes, use a chemical treatment (purification tablets), or filter it through a portable water filtering system.\" And: \"The average person drinks one quart of water per hour while hiking on a hot day. It''s important to plan ahead and bring plenty of water.\""},{"name":"Walkabout Outfitter, Harrisonburg","source":"https://www.walkaboutoutfitter.com/pages/harrisonburg-location-page","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"walk-in store (and walkaboutoutfitter.com)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":67,"blurb":"Outdoor clothing and gear retailer, 90 N. Main Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22802, 540-434-9900: outdoor apparel and gear including camping equipment, backpacking supplies, clothing and footwear. No rentals mentioned on the page read; Harrisonburg is a gateway city west of the park''s Swift Run Gap entrance, distance not stated on the page"}],"faq":[{"q":"Do I need a ticket for Shenandoah National Park?","a":"An entrance pass covers the park. Old Rag Mountain also needs its own day-use ticket from March 1 to November 30, including the Saddle, Ridge and Ridge Access trails: $2.00 per person of any age, sold only through Recreation.gov or 877-444-6777, separate from the entrance pass; 800 a day, 400 released 30 days ahead and 400 released 5 days ahead, at 10:00 a.m.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/planyourvisit/faqs-oldrag.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"How much does it cost to get into Shenandoah National Park?","a":"\"Private Vehicle $30.00\" for seven consecutive days, \"Motorcycle $25.00\", \"Per Person $15.00\" for walk-up or bicycling visitors 16 and older (children under 16 free), and \"Annual Entrance - Park $55.00\". Since July 1, 2025 the park \"accepts only mobile or electronic payments for entrance and campground fees.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When is Shenandoah National Park free?","a":"The park lists eight fee-free entrance days in 2026: February 16, May 25, June 14, July 3-5, August 25, September 17, October 27 (Theodore Roosevelt''s birthday) and November 11 (Veterans Day).","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you drive through Shenandoah National Park?","a":"Yes, on Skyline Drive, which \"runs 105 miles north and south along the crest of the Blue Ridge Mountains\", with a 35 mph limit in most places and four entrances. The NPS says \"most people need at least 3-4 hours to simply drive through\" the park.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When is peak foliage in Shenandoah National Park?","a":"The NPS: \"generally, fall colors seem to be at their most brilliant stage around the 2nd or 3rd week of October.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp in Shenandoah National Park?","a":"Yes. Campgrounds are booked through Recreation.gov: Big Meadows is reservation only; Mathews Arm and Loft Mountain have both reservable and first-come sites; Lewis Mountain is first-come, first-served with self-registration and \"Sites can not be reserved\". Backcountry camping needs a permit bought through Recreation.gov.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/planyourvisit/campground-reservations.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Is Shenandoah National Park part of the Appalachian Trail?","a":"Yes. The park has \"over 500 miles of hiking trails, including 101 miles of the Appalachian Trail\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where can I stay in Shenandoah National Park?","a":"\"All lodging facilities in Shenandoah National Park are operated by Delaware North, the Park concessionaire\": Skyland (mile 41.7), Big Meadows Lodge (mile 51) and Lewis Mountain Cabins (mile 57.5), booked at goshenandoah.com or 877-847-1919. The Potomac Appalachian Trail Club maintains six primitive cabins in the park.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/planyourvisit/lodging.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Is Shenandoah National Park open?","a":"The NPS: \"Shenandoah National Park is open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week\". Portions of Skyline Drive are periodically closed in inclement weather, and lodges, waysides and campgrounds are seasonal.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you bring dogs to Shenandoah National Park?","a":"Yes: \"Pets are allowed, if leashed, on most trails\" and in campgrounds, on \"a physical leash no longer than 6 feet at all times.\" Closed to pets are trails including Fox Hollow, Stony Man, Limberlost, the Old Rag Ridge and Saddle trails, Dark Hollow Falls, Bearfence Mountain and Frazier Discovery - \"fewer than 20 miles of the 500+ miles of trails\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/shen/planyourvisit/pets.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Shenandoah National Park: Skyline Drive, Old Rag & Valley Glamping | TravelWell","meta_description":"How Old Rag tickets work, when fall colour peaks, how each campground is reserved, and where to stay from Skyland to riverside yurts in Luray and Front Royal.","slug":"shenandoah-national-park-virginia","primary_keyword":"Shenandoah National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Shenandoah National Park, Virginia"}}'::jsonb, 39),
  ('liberty-new-jersey', '12A', 'Liberty State Park', 'United States', 'Statue of Liberty views and the Ellis Island ferry', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Mid-Atlantic', '{"culture","family","wildlife","ocean","parks"}', '{"historic","urban","coastal","family-friendly"}', '{}', null, null, '{"safety":{"posture":"book-freely","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","verified":"2026-10-08"},"jewels":[{"name":"Statue City Cruises ferry to the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island","source":"https://www.nps.gov/stli/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","family","senior","ocean"],"booking_route":"own website booking (statuecitycruises.com), ticket windows in the CRRNJ Terminal, or 1-877-LADYTIX (1-877-523-9849)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["move","activities"],"draw_rank":1,"blurb":"\"Statue City Cruises is the ONLY ferry service authorized by the National Park Service to sell tickets for, and provide transportation to Liberty and Ellis Islands\"; the New Jersey departure is \"the historic railroad terminal in Liberty State Park\". NPS-listed fares: adult (13+) $26.00, senior (62+) $23.00, child (4-12) $17.00, under 4 free; pedestal or crown access adds $0.30."},{"name":"Central Railroad of New Jersey (CRRNJ) Terminal","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260825062947/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/central-railroad-of-new-jersey-terminal/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","rail","family","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed to enter (\"Entrance Fee None\"); history programmes by pre-registration with the Nature Center, 201-915-3400 x503","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":2,"blurb":"\"Built in 1889, the Central Railroad of New Jersey (CRRNJ) Terminal stands as the cornerstone of Liberty State Park. It is listed on the State and National Registers of Historic Places.\" It welcomed \"new immigrants from Ellis Island\"; train service ceased in 1967 and the terminal \"now serves as a gateway for visitors to the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island.\" History programmes (Historic Trilogy, Explosion at Black Tom, Trail of the Blue Comet) run monthly with pre-registration."},{"name":"Statue of Liberty National Monument","source":"https://www.nps.gov/stli/index.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","family","senior","pilgrimage"],"booking_route":"reached only by the Statue City Cruises ferry; crown and pedestal by reservation with the ferry ticket","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":3,"blurb":"\"A gift of friendship from the people of France to the United States\", dedicated October 28, 1886. The Statue of Liberty Museum on Liberty Island holds \"artifacts and exhibits, including the original torch\"; crown and pedestal access need reservations. \"The National Park Service does not charge an entrance fee to visit the museums on Liberty Island and Ellis Island\" - the cost is the ferry."},{"name":"Empty Sky, 9/11 Memorial","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","pilgrimage","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - inside the park; NJDEP lists \"Entrance Fee: None\"","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":4,"blurb":"\"The official State of New Jersey Memorial that honors the memory of the 750 people that lived in or had ties to New Jersey that lost their lives\" on September 11, 2001. Twin stainless steel walls \"210 feet long, the width of each side of the World Trade Center Towers\", 30 feet high; designed by Jessica Jamroz and Frederic Schwartz, dedicated September 11, 2011."},{"name":"Ellis Island National Museum of Immigration","source":"https://www.nps.gov/elis/index.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","pilgrimage","family","senior"],"booking_route":"reached by the Statue City Cruises ferry from Liberty State Park or The Battery","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":5,"blurb":"\"A memorial to all who pursued the American dream and have made this nation their adopted home\"; over 12 million immigrants were processed here during 1892-1924. The Registry Room (the Great Hall) is where \"millions of immigrants were inspected\" and \"required to pass both a medical and legal inspection\"."},{"name":"Liberty Science Center","source":"https://lsc.org/plan-your-visit","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","culture"],"booking_route":"own website booking (lsc.org; best rates at least one day in advance); groups of 10+ on 201-253-1310 or groups@lsc.org","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":6,"blurb":"At 222 Jersey City Boulevard, home of the Jennifer Chalsty Planetarium and exhibits including Energy Quest, Our Hudson Home, Bees to Bots and Microbes Rule!; parking $7.00 for cars, 750 spaces with overflow at the nearby Light Rail lot; NJ Transit riders save $5 per person (up to 4 passes). Closed October 5-7, 2026. NJDEP calls its planetarium \"the largest planetarium in the western hemisphere\"."},{"name":"Hudson River Waterfront Walkway (Liberty State Park promenade)","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","hiking","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - free public promenade","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":7,"blurb":"\"A two-mile promenade, Hudson River Waterfront Walkway links two picnic and playground areas, the Nature Center and the CRRNJ Terminal while presenting visitors with a sweeping view of the Hudson River.\""},{"name":"Liberty Landing Ferry to Brookfield Place, Manhattan","source":"https://www.libertylandingcityferry.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","family"],"booking_route":"pay onboard (per NJDEP); 10-trip booklet $80 and monthly pass $320 per the operator","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["move"],"draw_rank":8,"blurb":"Runs between Liberty Landing Marina, Warren Street (Jersey City) and Brookfield Place Terminal, New York; one-way adult $10.00, children 7-12 $5.00, 6 and under free, seniors $6.00; weekdays 6:30am-7:30pm, weekends 9:30am-7:30pm, hourly. The boat docks at the marina behind Liberty House Restaurant, where parking is available. NJDEP: \"Fares are collected onboard.\""},{"name":"Richard J. Sullivan Natural Area","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","hiking","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - free public natural area","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":9,"blurb":"A 36-acre state Natural Area \"consisting mainly of salt marsh, one of the few remaining tidal marshes of the Hudson River Estuary\"; its berry-bearing shrubs and trees \"make the area a haven for many different species of birds\", with self-guided nature paths."},{"name":"The Nature Center at Liberty State Park","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"none needed to visit; programmes by email or phone with the Nature Center","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":10,"blurb":"\"An environmental and historical education facility located on Freedom Way. Open year-round the center features exhibits focusing on the natural history and ecology of the Hudson River Estuary\", open seven days a week, 8 a.m.-4 p.m.; contact LSPNatureCenter@dep.nj.gov or 201-915-3400 Option 4."},{"name":"Liberty Landing Marina","source":"http://libertylandingmarina.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["yacht","sailing","ocean"],"booking_route":"online transient booking via Molo (book.getmolo.com/libertylandingmarina/search) or (201) 985-8000","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","activities"],"draw_rank":11,"blurb":"At 80 Audrey Zapp Dr, operated by Suntex; contract and transient slips, a fuel dock, a marine service centre and store, and a Certified Clean Marina designation. NJDEP: \"250 slips, transient dockage, dry dock storage, a 24-hour fueling facility\"."},{"name":"9/11 Memorial & Museum, Lower Manhattan","source":"https://www.911memorial.org/visit","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","pilgrimage","senior"],"booking_route":"own website booking for the Museum (advance tickets); groups via reservations@911memorial.org or (212) 312-8800","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":12,"blurb":"At 180 Greenwich Street; honours nearly 3,000 people killed on September 11, 2001 and in the February 26, 1993 bombing. The Memorial is \"free and open to the public seven days a week\", daily 8 a.m.-8 p.m.; the Museum opens Wednesday-Monday 9 a.m.-7 p.m. (last entry 5:30 p.m.) with advance tickets. Reached from the park by the Liberty Landing Ferry to Brookfield Place."},{"name":"Sea the City jet ski tours, Liberty Landing Marina","source":"https://www.seathecity.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","ocean"],"booking_route":"Peek (book.peek.com); phone (201) 335-2732","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":13,"blurb":"Departs Liberty Landing Marina, 84 Audrey Zapp Dr: \"Sea The Highlights: 1-Hour Jet Ski Tour\" from $185 and \"Sea It All: 2-2.5 Hour Jet Ski Tour\" from $335; \"No Experience Necessary\", ages 10+ with parent or guardian, maximum 9 guests per tour; also a hot tub boat tour."},{"name":"Liberty State Park picnic areas and pavilions","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","group"],"booking_route":"pavilions and group areas by application to libertystatepark@dep.nj.gov or 201-915-3400 Option 2; small groups first-come","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":14,"blurb":"Groups of 20 or fewer need no permit and may bring their own charcoal grill; seven Open-Air Group Picnic Areas (20-50 people) by free permit; Pavilion A (up to 120) $200 NJ resident / $250 non-resident and Pavilion B (up to 80) $150 / $200. \"No propane grills, wood fires, generators\"; no alcohol; \"Wedding receptions/ceremonies are not permitted in the park.\""},{"name":"Fishing and crabbing on Upper New York Bay","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"none needed at the park; NJ Saltwater Recreational Registry Program applies","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":15,"blurb":"\"The Upper New York Bay and Hudson River offer excellent opportunities for fishing. Common species include bluefish, shad, striped bass and blue claw crabs.\" Permitted under NJ Fish and Wildlife laws; \"Consumption advisories may exist for certain species.\""},{"name":"Boat launch and car-top kayak launch","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","adventure","sailing"],"booking_route":"permits at the park office or the Parking Lot 2 ticket machine; car-top launch free","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":16,"blurb":"The trailered-boat launch in Parking Lot 2 runs 6 a.m.-10 p.m. year-round with mandatory permits (max trailer 23 ft); daily launch $20 NJ resident / $25 non-resident, seasonal $170 / $200. Kayaks and canoes launch from the East Jetty by Parking Lot 4 with \"No permit required, no fee\"."},{"name":"Maddy Rose, Liberty Landing","source":"https://bylandmark.com/restaurants/maddy-rose/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"OpenTable; phone (201) 395-0300","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":17,"blurb":"\"Where bold flavors meet unbeatable waterfront city views\": steaks, seafood and Mediterranean-inspired coastal cuisine with a Wine Spectator award-winning wine list, at 76 Audrey Zapp Dr; lunch Wed-Fri 12-3pm and Sat-Sun 11am-3pm, dinner Wed-Sun."},{"name":"The Feathered Fox, Liberty Landing","source":"https://www.thefeatheredfox.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"online reservation form on own website; phone (201) 419-6791","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":18,"blurb":"\"Executive Chef Chris Siversen and the team behind Jersey City''s Maritime Parc\" reinvent the steakhouse \"with stops that include inventive sushi and an exquisite raw bar\", at 84 Audrey Zapp Drive."},{"name":"Razza Pizza Artigianale, Jersey City","source":"https://www.razzanj.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"OpenTable; phone 201-356-9348","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":19,"blurb":"Wood-burning-oven pizza, small plates, beer, wine and seasonal cocktails at 275-277 Grove Street; NJ Monthly: \"This stylish 40-seat restaurant serves one of the best wood-fired pizzas we''ve ever had.\" Mon-Thu 5-10pm, Fri-Sat 3-10pm, Sun 3-9pm."},{"name":"Liberty House Restaurant","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["romance","culinary","group"],"booking_route":"phone 201-395-0300 or info@landmarkhospitality.com","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":20,"blurb":"A park tenant at 76 Audrey Zapp Drive, named by NJDEP as one of the designated places where weddings and receptions may be held in the park; the marina describes it as offering \"one of the region''s most iconic settings for weddings, celebrations, corporate gatherings, and private events.\""},{"name":"Maritime Parc","source":"https://www.maritimeparc.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["romance","culinary","group"],"booking_route":"phone (201) 413-0050, info@maritimeparc.com or online enquiry form","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":21,"blurb":"At 84 Audrey Zapp Drive in the park: a waterfront venue with a \"280-degree wraparound terrace\" overlooking the New York skyline and the Hudson River, with menus built on seasonal ingredients; NJDEP names \"The Restaurant at Maritime Parc\" as a park wedding tenant."},{"name":"Nathan''s Famous Hot Dogs, Liberty Landing","source":"http://libertylandingmarina.com/attractions/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","culinary"],"booking_route":"walk-up, no booking","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":22,"blurb":"\"Serving up World Famous Hot Dogs, Fresh Angus Burgers, Hand-dipped Chicken and more\" on the far side of Liberty House; Thursday and Sunday 12-6pm, Friday and Saturday 12-7pm, May-October, weather dependent."},{"name":"Liberty Harbor RV Park, Jersey City","source":"https://www.libertyharborrv.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","overland","family"],"booking_route":"CampLife (camplife.com) or (201) 516-7500","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":23,"blurb":"An urban RV park at 11 Marin Blvd with \"Water + 30A/50A electric\" at each site and on-site dump stations (no individual sewer); \"Nightly rates start at $170\" with a 50% non-refundable deposit; \"2 PATH stops to World Trade Center from Grove Street\"."},{"name":"Hyatt Regency Jersey City on the Hudson","source":"https://www.visithudson.org/things-to-do/hotels/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","romance"],"booking_route":"hyatt.com (brand booking; not fetched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":24,"blurb":"Listed by Hudson County tourism under Jersey City (\"6 miles from NYC\"), which singles out \"the Hyatt Regency''s waterfront vistas in Jersey City\". The brand''s own page refused the fetch (HTTP 403)."},{"name":"Hyatt House Jersey City","source":"https://www.visithudson.org/things-to-do/hotels/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"hyatt.com (brand booking; not fetched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":25,"blurb":"Listed by Hudson County tourism under Jersey City, which names \"the luxe Hyatt House''s sweeping Lower Manhattan views\". The brand''s own page refused the fetch (HTTP 403)."},{"name":"The Westin Jersey City Newport","source":"https://www.visithudson.org/things-to-do/hotels/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["senior","family"],"booking_route":"marriott.com (brand booking; not fetched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":26,"blurb":"Listed by Hudson County tourism among Jersey City hotels (\"6 miles from NYC\"). Marriott''s own page refused the fetch (HTTP 403), so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Canopy by Hilton Jersey City Arts District","source":"https://www.visithudson.org/things-to-do/hotels/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","romance"],"booking_route":"hilton.com (brand booking; not fetched - HTTP 403)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"Listed by Hudson County tourism among Jersey City hotels (\"6 miles from NYC\"). Hilton''s own page refused the fetch (HTTP 403), so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Collective Governors Island","source":"https://www.collectiveretreats.com/retreat/collective-governors-island/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","romance","family"],"booking_route":"own website booking (collectiveretreats.book.pegsbe.com) or 646-572-5341","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"Glamping on Governors Island in New York Harbor - Voyager and Urban Cowboy tents, Basecamp Cabins (including ADA units) and suites - with \"dreamlike views of the Statue of Liberty\"; \"Open seasonally from May to November\", an 8-minute ferry from Battery Maritime Terminal in Manhattan."},{"name":"Sandy Hook Campground (Gateway National Recreation Area)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/gate/planyourvisit/camping-at-gateway.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","ocean","group"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov (Camp Gateway Sandy Hook listing)","commission_status":"none","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"Tent camping only (\"RVs cannot be accommodated\"), May-September 2026: standard sites up to 6 people $30/night ($15 with Senior/Access Pass), larger sites up to 10 people $50, group sites $150; maximum 14 consecutive nights; \"Alcohol, pets, and charcoal grills are NOT allowed at tent camping sites.\""},{"name":"Picnic kit for Liberty State Park lawns: blankets, camp chairs, a sunshade and a charcoal grill","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","group"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"NJ State Parks: \"Groups of 20 people or less may also picnic on the grass, using their own blankets and camping chairs. A maximum of one Sunshade or canopy, no bigger than 10′ x 10′ is allowed per group. Small groups may bring their own charcoal grill\"; \"All spent coal must be disposed of in the designated ''Hot Coal'' dumping bins.\""},{"name":"Tick protection for the park''s trails and natural area","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","hiking","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"NJ State Parks rules for Liberty State Park, Tick Protection: \"Use insect repellent, wear light-colored clothing, tuck pants into socks, stay on trails, check yourself when you get home, shower and wash clothes immediately.\""},{"name":"Fishing and crabbing kit for Upper New York Bay","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":3,"commission_pct_high":3,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"NJ State Parks: \"The Upper New York Bay and Hudson River offer excellent opportunities for fishing. Common species include bluefish, shad, striped bass and blue claw crabs. Fishing and crabbing are permitted in accordance with NJ Fish and Wildlife laws.\" \"Please dispose of all stray fishing line properly.\""},{"name":"Paddling kit for the car-top kayak launch","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","ocean"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"NJ State Parks: \"Car-top Boats (Kayaks, Canoes) No permit required, no fee. Car-top boats can be launched from the car-top boat launch located at the East Jetty by Parking Lot 4. Hours of operations are 6 a.m. to 10 p.m.\""}],"faq":[{"q":"Is there a ferry from Liberty State Park to the Statue of Liberty?","a":"Yes. NJDEP: \"Ferry service from Liberty State Park to the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island is available throughout the year. For rates, ferry schedules, and to purchase tickets online please visit Statue City Cruises'' website or call 1-877-LADY-TIX or 877-523-9849. Tickets may also be purchased at the ticket window inside the CRRNJ Terminal Building.\"","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How do I get to Ellis Island from Liberty State Park?","a":"By the Statue City Cruises ferry from the historic railroad terminal in the park. The NPS states that \"Statue City Cruises is the ONLY ferry service authorized by the National Park Service to sell tickets for, and provide transportation to Liberty and Ellis Islands\", and warns against buying from third-party vendors offering higher prices or non-landing boats.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/stli/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How do I get to Liberty State Park from NYC by ferry?","a":"The Liberty Landing Ferry runs between Brookfield Place Terminal in New York, Warren Street in Jersey City and Liberty Landing Marina in the park, weekdays 6:30am-7:30pm and weekends 9:30am-7:30pm. One-way fares: adult $10.00, children 7-12 $5.00, seniors $6.00, 6 and under free. The boat docks at the marina behind Liberty House Restaurant.","source":"https://www.libertylandingcityferry.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Liberty State Park free?","a":"There is no entrance fee: NJDEP lists \"Entrance Fee: None\". Fees apply to the picnic pavilions, the trailered-boat launch and the ferries, not to entering the park.","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When does Liberty State Park close?","a":"NJDEP lists the gate hours as 6am-10pm, with the Park Office open 8am-4pm daily.","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you fish at Liberty State Park?","a":"Yes. \"Fishing and crabbing are permitted in accordance with NJ Fish and Wildlife laws.\" Common species include \"bluefish, shad, striped bass and blue claw crabs\", and \"Consumption advisories may exist for certain species.\"","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you grill at Liberty State Park?","a":"Charcoal only. \"Small groups may bring their own charcoal grill, whether picnicking at our tables, or on the grass. All spent coal must be disposed of in the designated ''Hot Coal'' dumping bins.\" The picnic rules also state: \"No propane grills, wood fires, generators or access to electrical outlets.\"","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Liberty State Park dog friendly?","a":"Pets are allowed on a leash: \"Pets must always be on a leash no longer than six feet in length and under the control of the owner. Please clean up after your pets.\"","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Liberty State Park a national park?","a":"No. It is a New Jersey state park, published by the Department of Environmental Protection under State Parks, Forests & Historic Sites, with its office in the CRRNJ Terminal Building, 1 Audrey Zapp Drive, Jersey City. The Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island, reached by ferry from the park, are National Park Service sites.","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you smoke in Liberty State Park?","a":"No. \"State law prohibits the smoking of tobacco and use of electronic smoking (vaping) devices in all state parks, forests, historic sites, recreation areas, golf courses and marinas.\"","source":"http://web.archive.org/web/20260919222450/https://dep.nj.gov/parksandforests/state-park/liberty-state-park/","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Liberty State Park, NJ: Statue of Liberty Ferry, CRRNJ Terminal & Jersey City | TravelWell","meta_description":"No entrance fee, the only New Jersey ferry to the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island, the CRRNJ Terminal, Empty Sky memorial and Liberty Science Center.","slug":"liberty-state-park-new-jersey","primary_keyword":"Liberty State Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Liberty State Park Statue of Liberty view"}}'::jsonb, 40)
