ission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"35200 S. Dixie Hwy., Florida City: outdoor pool and \"hot breakfast buffet\", 2.5 miles from downtown Homestead per the listing. Sourced to Priceline''s Homestead hotel listing; the hotel''s own site did not connect."},{"name":"Robert Is Here","source":"https://www.robertishere.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"19200 SW 344th St, Homestead: \"The World''s Best Fruit Stand\" since 1959 - fresh produce, handmade milkshakes and smoothies, a petting zoo and picnic areas; open daily 9am-6pm (closed Thanksgiving and Christmas). (305) 246-1592."},{"name":"Black Point Ocean Grill","source":"https://www.blackpointoceangrill.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","ocean"],"booking_route":"phone 305-258-3918 (no reservation method on the page)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"24775 S.W. 87th Avenue, Cutler Bay, at Black Point Marina: \"fresh seafood, produce, hand cut steaks, salads and sandwiches\" on the water; open daily from 11am, to midnight Friday and Saturday. 305-258-3918."},{"name":"Schnebly Redland''s Winery & Brewery","source":"https://www.schneblywinery.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"OpenTable for the restaurant; tastings and tours on the own site","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","activities"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"30205 SW 217th Ave, Homestead: \"The southernmost winery in the United States\", tropical fruit wines, an on-site brewery and a thatched tiki restaurant; wine tasting $25, winery tour $16, combo $41. (305) 242-1224."},{"name":"Shiver''s BBQ","source":"https://www.shiversbbq.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in; phone (305) 248-2272","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"28001 S Dixie Hwy, Homestead: \"Since 1950\" - \"slow smoked ribs, brisket, pulled pork and Southern sides\", hickory-smoked. (305) 248-2272."},{"name":"The Fish House Restaurant and Seafood Market","source":"https://www.fishhouse.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","ocean"],"booking_route":"walk-in - no reservations","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"102401 Overseas Highway, Key Largo: \"the finest seafood available\" with daily catches and an on-site seafood market that will \"cook your catch\"; \"No reservations needed, just come on in\". 305.451.4665."},{"name":"Key Largo Conch House","source":"https://www.keylargoconchhouse.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","group","tropical"],"booking_route":"walk-in; group reservations by phone 305-453-4844","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"100211 Overseas Hwy, Key Largo: \"Fresh Local Seafood and Produce\" and \"homemade desserts\" at breakfast, lunch and dinner; breakfast 8-11 am weekdays, dinner from 4 pm daily. 305-453-4844."},{"name":"Coral Castle Museum","source":"https://coralcastle.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","family","romance"],"booking_route":"tickets at the gate or on the own site (admission not read)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"28655 S. Dixie Highway, Homestead: an \"architectural marvel constructed single-handedly by Edward Leedskalnin from 1923 to 1951\" from limestone blocks; open daily 9AM-8PM, last tour 7:00PM. (305) 248-6345."},{"name":"Reef-safe sun protection for Biscayne''s reefs and wrecks","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","diveglobal","tropical","sailing"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":35,"blurb":"NPS, Biscayne safety page: \"You can help protect yourself AND the resources of Biscayne National Park by using ''Reef-Safe Sun Protection''.\" Pack a reef-safe sunscreen before the boat, snorkel or paddle day."},{"name":"UV-blocking water clothing, polarized glasses and hats","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["ocean","sailing","diveglobal","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to amazon.com (Amazon Associates); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":4,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":36,"blurb":"NPS, Biscayne safety page, alongside reef-safe sun protection: \"or UV blocking clothing designed for the water. Things like polarized glasses and hats can also be helpful.\""},{"name":"Drinking water and insect protection for Boca Chita and Elliott Key camping","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/planyourvisit/camping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["tropical","sailing","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":37,"blurb":"NPS camping page: \"Drinking water is available, but bring water as a precaution if the system goes down.\" \"Insects – May be prevalent year round. Expect heavy populations of insects during the warmer months.\" Elliott Key: \"Mosquitoes and no-see-ums (biting midges) are prevalent year round.\""}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Biscayne National Park free?","a":"Entry is free: \"The park has no entrance fees.\" Docking is charged - \"$25.00 Friday - Monday and Federal Holidays\" for day use, and \"$60.00 per night\" for overnight camping and docking.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Do you need a boat to get to Biscayne National Park?","a":"For most of it, yes: \"the park is 95% water\", and \"the coral reefs are over ten miles from the mainland by boat, so please consider one of the snorkel tours.\" The Dante Fascell Visitor Center and Convoy Point grounds are reached by car.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How do I get to Biscayne National Park?","a":"The visitor center is at \"9700 SW 328th Street, Sir Lancelot Jones Way, Homestead, FL 33033\". From the Florida Turnpike take Exit 6 (Speedway Boulevard), turn left to SW 328th Street and go four miles to the park entrance; from US 1 northbound turn right on SW 344th Street (Palm Drive), then right on SW 328th Street and \"Continue for four miles to the end of the road.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp at Biscayne National Park?","a":"Yes, on Elliott Key and Boca Chita Key, but \"The only access to these islands is by boat\" and \"No reservations may be made in advance for these campgrounds; they are available on a first-come, first-served basis.\" Overnight camping and docking is $60 a night.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/planyourvisit/camping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What tours are there in Biscayne National Park?","a":"The Biscayne National Park Institute runs \"eco-adventures including snorkeling at a shipwreck on the Maritime Heritage Trail and colorful coral reefs full of life, cruises to Boca Chita Key and lighthouse, sailing on beautiful Biscayne Bay, exploring the seldom seen wonders of Jones Lagoon\". Book online, on 786-335-3644 or at the park store; \"Advance reservations are advised.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/planyourvisit/guidedtours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you fish in Biscayne National Park?","a":"Yes: \"With limited exceptions, a valid Florida fishing license is required to fish in the park. Children under 16 years of age do not require a license.\" Fishing is prohibited in the harbors, docks and picnic areas at Boca Chita Key, Elliott Key and Convoy Point.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/planyourvisit/fishing.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you catch lobster in Biscayne National Park?","a":"Only outside the protected areas: \"The taking of lobster is prohibited in the Biscayne Bay/Card Sound Lobster Sanctuary including all natural, artificial and tidal creeks between the islands and along the mainland\", and in five Coral Reef Protection Areas marked with yellow buoys. The NPS points to its lobstering page for full rules.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/planyourvisit/fishing.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Biscayne National Park dog friendly?","a":"In part. Pets are allowed on \"The grounds at Convoy Point\" and \"Elliott Key\", but not on \"Boca Chita Key, including on boats docked in the harbor\" or in \"The Dante Fascell Visitor Center\". \"Pets must be kept on a leash no longer than 6 feet and under your control at all times.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/planyourvisit/pets.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where can you see manatees in Biscayne National Park?","a":"The NPS says: \"yes, ask a park ranger about recent sightings. Manatees are more common during the colder months.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When is Biscayne National Park open?","a":"The Dante Fascell Visitor Center \"is open 7 days a week from 9 AM-5 PM\"; the Convoy Point grounds and canoe/kayak launch are \"open 7 days a week from 7 AM-5:30 PM\"; the navigable waters are \"Open 24 hours a day\"; Adams Key is \"Open 9 AM until official sunset daily\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/bisc/planyourvisit/hours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Biscayne National Park: Reefs, Boca Chita & Shipwrecks | TravelWell","meta_description":"Free entry, a 95% water park off Miami: boat-in camping on Boca Chita and Elliott Key, six wrecks on the Maritime Heritage Trail, and tours from Homestead.","slug":"biscayne-national-park-florida","primary_keyword":"Biscayne National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Boca Chita Key lighthouse Biscayne National Park"}}'::jsonb, 43)
