 essentials list: \"Insulation (jacket, hat, gloves, layers, & rain gear)\"; \"Wear suitable hiking shoes or boots with good ankle support.\""},{"name":"Headlamp - \"your phone does not count\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsm/planyourvisit/hikingsafety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":7,"commission_pct_high":7,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":64,"blurb":"The NPS essentials list: \"Illumination (flashlight or headlamp; your phone does not count)\" and \"Navigation (map, compass, & GPS)\"."},{"name":"NOC Gatlinburg - The Great Outpost","source":"https://noc.com/gatlinburg/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in store","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":65,"blurb":"Nantahala Outdoor Center''s Gatlinburg store at 1138 Parkway, Gatlinburg, TN 37738: \"18,000 square feet of outdoor gear from top brands like The North Face and Patagonia, local goods and gifts, everything needed to enjoy an adventure into the Smokies\", with boot fitting and help choosing hiking and camping gear"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Great Smoky Mountains National Park free?","a":"Entry is free: \"Great Smoky Mountains National Park does not charge an entrance fee.\" But \"Parking tags are required for all vehicles parking for longer than 15 minutes\": Daily $5, Weekly $15, Annual $40 in 2026, sold on recreation.gov and at automated machines. Vehicles with state-issued disability placards or plates are exempt.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsm/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What is the best time to visit Great Smoky Mountains National Park for fall colors?","a":"\"Typically, the last three weeks of October are the best time of year to view fall colors.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsm/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How busy is Great Smoky Mountains National Park?","a":"The NPS says it draws \"around 12 million visitors a year,\" making it \"the most visited national park in the country.\" \"The park typically experiences peak visitation between 9 AM and 2 PM\"; in busy seasons it advises entering \"no later than 8 AM\" or \"around 3 PM.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsm/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp in Great Smoky Mountains National Park?","a":"Yes, at 10 developed frontcountry campgrounds. \"Advance reservations are required\" through Recreation.gov or 877-444-6777. Cades Cove and Smokemont are open year-round and the rest seasonally; stays are limited to 14 consecutive days and six people per site.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsm/planyourvisit/frontcountry-camping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Can you stay in the Smoky Mountains National Park?","a":"Beyond the campgrounds, LeConte Lodge on Mount LeConte calls itself \"the highest guest lodge in the eastern United States\", at about 6,400 feet. It is reachable only on foot, by trails of 5 to 9.1 miles, and opens from late March to mid-November. Reservations are made directly with the lodge.","source":"https://www.lecontelodge.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Is Great Smoky Mountains National Park dog friendly?","a":"Only in some places. Pets are allowed \"In frontcountry campgrounds\", \"In picnic areas\", \"Along roadways\" and \"On two dog-friendly trails—the Gatlinburg Trail and the Oconaluftee River Trail\", and \"must be kept on a leash no longer than 6 feet at all times.\" Other trails are off-limits to pets.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsm/planyourvisit/pets.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you fish in Great Smoky Mountains National Park?","a":"Yes: \"Fishing is permitted year-round in open waters from 30 minutes before official sunrise to 30 minutes after official sunset.\" Anglers 16 and older need \"a valid fishing license or permit from either Tennessee or North Carolina\", and \"Only artificial flies or lures with a single hook may be used.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsm/planyourvisit/fishing.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is the closest airport to Great Smoky Mountains National Park?","a":"On the Tennessee side, \"McGhee-Tyson Airport (TYS) located just south of Knoxville in Alcoa... approximately 45 miles west of the Gatlinburg entrance.\" On the North Carolina side, \"Asheville Regional Airport is located approximately 60 miles east of the Cherokee entrance to the park.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsm/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When was Great Smoky Mountains National Park established?","a":"\"Great Smoky Mountains National Park was founded in 1934.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsm/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Great Smoky Mountains: Cades Cove, Kuwohi & Elk | TravelWell","meta_description":"No entrance fee, a $5 parking tag, October colour, the elk rut and the firefly lottery, plus the gateway towns and stays around America''s most visited park.","slug":"great-smoky-mountains-national-park-tennessee","primary_keyword":"Great Smoky Mountains National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Great Smoky Mountains National Park, Cades Cove"}}'::jsonb, 47),
