for the gorge trails","source":"https://www.nps.gov/neri/planyourvisit/hiking-safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":47,"blurb":"The NPS hiking-safety page: \"Wear appropriate clothes and shoes for hiking.\" \"Carry rain gear; sudden thunderstorms can occur at any time.\""},{"name":"Water and trail snacks for longer hikes","source":"https://www.nps.gov/neri/planyourvisit/hiking-safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":48,"blurb":"The NPS: \"Bring water and drink regularly; bring snacks or lunch for longer hikes.\" Also: \"During spring and summer, check for ticks.\""},{"name":"Water Stone Outdoors, Fayetteville","source":"https://www.waterstoneoutdoors.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","sports"],"booking_route":"walk-in store (rentals on site)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":49,"blurb":"\"Water Stone Outdoors has been selling outdoor gear and apparel in Fayetteville, WV since 1994\": climbing gear, camping gear, apparel and books, plus rentals and consignment; 101 East Wiseman Avenue, Fayetteville, WV 25840, 304-574-2425"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is New River Gorge National Park free?","a":"Yes. The NPS states: \"New River Gorge National Park and Preserve does not charge an entrance fee.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/neri/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Can you camp at New River Gorge National Park?","a":"Yes. The NPS lists park campgrounds including Stone Cliff Beach, Army Camp, Grandview Sandbar and Glade Creek, with \"no camping fees at park campgrounds\"; \"Reservations are not available; all sites are first-come, first-serve.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/neri/planyourvisit/camping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Can you walk on the New River Gorge Bridge?","a":"Yes, with Bridge Walk: a harnessed walk on the catwalk \"25 feet beneath the New River Gorge Bridge\", year-round from $79, for ages 8 and up and at least 48 inches tall. The NPS names it \"the only company that take visitors on the bridge\".","source":"https://www.bridgewalk.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"What is the best time to visit New River Gorge National Park?","a":"It depends on the activity. The NPS gives climbing as best \"late April to mid-June\" and \"mid-September to late October\"; the Gauley''s \"main season is early-September through mid-October\" and New River rafting runs \"April through October\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/neri/planyourvisit/climbing.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Is New River Gorge National Park dog friendly?","a":"Yes: \"Pets are allowed on all trails at New River Gorge National Park and Preserve.\" They \"must always be on a physical leash no longer than 6 feet\", and \"Pets are not allowed in any park buildings or visitor centers\" or at ranger-led programs.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/neri/planyourvisit/pets.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you fish in New River Gorge National Park?","a":"Yes: \"Fishing is one of the most popular activities on the New River.\" \"All persons fishing in the park are required to have a West Virginia fishing license.\" The NPS names bass, walleye, muskellunge, crappie, bluegill, carp and catfish.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/neri/planyourvisit/fishing.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is the closest airport to New River Gorge National Park?","a":"\"Charleston WV, approximately 70 miles northwest of the park, is the closest major airport. Some flights are also available nearby at Beckley WV.\" Highway access is \"from Route 19, between Beckley and Hico, and from I-64, between Mossy and Sandstone.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/neri/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Are there hotels in New River Gorge National Park?","a":"No: \"The park does not have any lodging facilities, but motels, cabins, and bed & breakfasts are available in surrounding towns.\" The NPS adds that \"Hawks Nest and Pipestem Resort State Parks have lodges\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/neri/planyourvisit/eatingsleeping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where can you eat near New River Gorge National Park?","a":"Not inside the park. The NPS says: \"Restaurants and grocery stores can be found in Beckley, Fayetteville, Sandstone, Glen Jean, Oak Hill, Mount Hope, Beaver, Hinton, and other towns around the park.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/neri/planyourvisit/eatingsleeping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"New River Gorge National Park: Bridge, Bridge Day, Rafting & Climbing | TravelWell","meta_description":"A free West Virginia national park: the 876-foot bridge, Bridge Day, Lower New and Gauley rafting, 1,400+ climbs, free camping and glamping near Fayetteville.","slug":"new-river-gorge-national-park-west-virginia","primary_keyword":"New River Gorge National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"New River Gorge Bridge, West Virginia"}}'::jsonb, 48)
